Security final (fast-path) verdict: ACCEPT (scope: KMS/HMAC deployment & rotation proof; analytics aggregate-overflow attestation). Security validated artifacts (kms_deploy_proof, kms_audit_ingest_proof, kms_rotation_simulation, analytics_owner_attestation, etl_canary_output, aggregate_stress_test_logs, docs) and found no show-stopper in that scope. Remaining operational follow-ups for Ops/Analytics before final cutover: enable periodic KMS ACL reconciliation and rotation-simulation CI jobs, ensure KMS audit ingestion/alerts, reproduce ETL canary in the target env and retain analytics owner attestation, enable aggregation alerting/runbooks, and run a pre-deploy scan for dependent services doing unprotected 64-bit aggregations.

Request of ResponsibleAI (please respond with concrete answers):
A) Fairness/auditability review: Do you have any ethical/responsibility concerns given the security findings and provided artifacts? Specifically evaluate: reproducibility for dispute resolution, rounding/truncation impacts across locales or on vulnerable groups, transparency of canonicalization/HMAC for customer disputes, and whether user-facing disclosures or protections are needed.
B) Blocking status: Are any of the remaining operational items (KMS deployment reconciliation, analytics attestation/ETL canary reproduction, monitoring/runbooks) blocking from a ResponsibleAI perspective? If so, which and why?
C) Acceptance criteria: Provide explicit, measurable gating criteria you require before approving progression to Merger/DevOps (examples you can adopt or modify):
  - Minimum audit-log retention period (e.g., 12 months) and proof of ingestion/alerting; 
  - Reproducibility SLA for recalculations (e.g., deterministic recalculation within X minutes/using canonical library);
  - Declared rounding/truncation policy (quantize to 2 decimal places) and user-notification/errata process for billing differences; 
  - Dispute-resolution runbook availability and evidence HMAC/audit supports independent verification; 
  - Analytics-owner attestations for downstream consumers plus ETL-canary artifact reproduction in target env. 
Please state which of the above (or alternatives) you require and any numeric thresholds.
D) Re-review scope: Do you want Security to re-check only the two fast-path artifacts (Ops KMS reconciliation proof + Analytics ETL-canary reproduction/attestation) or perform a full re-review after all remediations? Also list any additional evidence/controls you require as gating conditions (e.g., retention windows, public/tenant-facing rounding disclosure, canonicalization library distribution to clients).

Please respond with: (1) blocking? yes/no (and why), (2) explicit acceptance criteria you require, and (3) preferred re-review scope.
